    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "You can use the equation of a function to write an equation for its transformation. For example, let \\(f(x) = x^2\\). Take the graph of \\(f\\), reflect it across the \\(x\\)-axis, translate it up 10 units, and translate it left 3 units. What…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Which means \\(g(x) =\\text-(x+3)^2 + 10\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes you can recognize from the expression for a function that it is the transformation of a simpler function. For example, consider:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle H(t) = 10 - (1.2)^{t+5}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "One way to obtain the expression for \\(H\\) from \\(1.2^t\\) is:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "adding 5 to the input to get \\((1.2)^{t+5}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "multiplying the output by -1 to get \\(\\text-(1.2)^{t+5}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
