      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "adding 10 to the output to get \\(10 - (1.2)^{t+5}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "So the graph of \\(H\\) is obtained from the graph of \\(f(t) = 1.2^t\\) by translating left 5 units, reflecting across the \\(x\\)-axis, and translating up 10 units. Consider the point \\((0,1)\\) on the graph of \\(f\\). After translating,…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A function \\(f\\) that satisfies the condition \\(f(x) = f(\\text-x)\\) for all inputs \\(x\\). You can tell an even function from its graph: Its graph is symmetric about the \\(y\\)-axis.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L07-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "7.3: An Even Better Fit",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A function \\(f\\) that satisfies \\(f(x) = \\text-f(\\text-x)\\) for all inputs \\(x\\). You can tell an odd function from its graph: Its graph is taken to itself when you reflect it across both the \\(x\\)- and \\(y\\)-axes. This can also be seen as…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u05-l07.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
